      "Language": "cze",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Saliva has a broad diagnostic potential which can be used for detection many pathological conditions including renal dysfunction. In saliva can be measured concentration of urea and creatinine as well as the other uremic markers. Saliva urea nitrogen and creatinine and blood urea and creatinine highly correlated therefore might be used for screening in patients with CKD. Saliva collection is truly non-invasive and is especially suitable for small children and elderly patients. Recently, semiquantitative saliva urea test strip is available. Saliva might become promising dia-gnostic biofluid in nephrological practice.Key words: chronic kidney disease - renal failure - salivary dipstick - salivary markers."},
